  "_gneuwit_is_pale": "A deliberate pale, not a dark. His WIT 疲勞－虛弱－貧血 is modern uwit 疲累（疲勞）— the map already carries wit→uwit, mawit→meuwit, kawit→keuwit, three slots agreeing — but the gn- slot of his § Gnwit na nanak ka sapax nii! 「這房子完全是他辛勞的代價」 had been left standing as his own gnwit, which is his spelling wearing modern clothes: the modern root has an initial u. Vowel-initial roots take the schwa between prefix and root — gneabu, gneabuh, gneaga are the shape, and this family writes it itself in kneuwit 辛苦 and mnegeuwit — so gn- + uwit is gneuwit. Nothing lists gneuwit, so it stays pale and the pair stays blocked; what the pin buys is that the card no longer says two different things about one root. Note the head is a homophone trap: bare wit IS listed, as 繩轉聲 and 逃走（旋即就逃）, neither of them his. [b196]",
  "_ilrdf_names": "The twenty below are spelled by the Council of Indigenous Peoples' name register (indigenous-name.ilrdf.org.tw, 太魯閣族, harvested to ilrdf_names.json), not by a gloss — a name has no gloss, so this file's usual test cannot be run on one. The rule: his own form is absent from the register, exactly ONE registered name of an AGREEING TYPE (his name (m) against 男名 or 男女共名, his name (f) against 女名 or 男女共名) is one edit away from the spelling his token puts on screen, and he declares the word a name himself. The type test is the load-bearing one: it is what refuses `miheng` (his name (f), Mihing 男名), and a token with no tag of his — tier N flags names off capitalisation — has no type to agree with and is never taken, which is what keeps `xane` out (it is not a name at all, it is a token in the example ASO NA SAO'LE XANE under the possessive prefix N). Where two registered names of an agreeing type are equally close the name is not identified and his spelling stands: `akit` has six, `ingay` has three and none of them 男名. His -Cwi names (ATWI, APWI, SIDWI, SIPWI) are left alone as a set — four of his names sharing a shape the register lacks is a spelling convention, not four slips, and SIDWI and SIPWI would both collapse onto Siwi and lose a distinction his book makes.",
  "_ma_iso": "His Ma\"iso (TABWI › Ptabwi, § Ma\"iso ka tmabwi! Ya xan! Ptbwiun mo ka laqe da! 「絕不能是你下去！等一下！我要派我的兒子下去。」) is two modern words, not one. The \" is his syllable break — the same mark stands inside Ma\"so and Ma\"lu — and here it falls on a word boundary: ma + isu. Both halves are listed and glossed, ma 問語（疑問助詞）and isu 你 (f481), and the parquets open 182 sentences with it in exactly this force: ma so kmpais mnan? 「為什麼要敵視我？」, ma so ini lahang tntakan? 「你怎麼沒有做防火線。」 A rhetorical ma-question IS a refusal, which is why his French renders it Pas question que ce soit toi qui déscende! and not as a question at all. A two-word value is a supported value: attested() splits on the space and requires every part verified, the mechanism built for A sao. Nothing here is maa- 成為 — his Ma\"so is masu 小米, not maasu, so the mark is not a long vowel; and the listed maaisu 「…像你一樣」 would say the son goes down BEING LIKE YOU. [b196]",
  "_pk_alternation": "Pecoraro documents this himself, in three entries: DUK 「請注意詞尾輔音P與K之間常見的變換；派生詞保留P，而詞基往往作K」, NDUP 「NDUK 的變體（詞尾的 P 實現為 K ＝ 常見的音變現象）」, GALUK 「相當多的詞基實際上容許 P 與 K 互換」. It is NOT a blanket rule — most of his final P is real P — so the gate is the one regular() uses: respell only where the K-twin is LISTED and its gloss agrees with his. Five values pass; `dup` itself does not, because bare `duk` is unlisted, and an unlisted respelling would buy a false dark. Keyed on his RAW tokens [batch 155].",
  "_psilin_is_psiling": "REFUSED, and the reason is mechanical. His sub Psilin sits under his own headword SILING, so the ng is his; but a key psilin->psiling reads to the cross-entry root projection as \"append g\", and it re-applied that to his RAW psiling (3x) and mpsiling, putting psilingg and empsilingg on the page. It bought 1 dark and cost 4. The single pale psilin stays pale. A respelling that is right about the word can still be wrong about the machine.",
  "_qapah_vowel": "Ruled by a Truku speaker, 2026-08-02: qapah is STICK, and it is not qpah. The two roots differ by the vowel and his typewriter syncopated it away, so PSQPAHAN/PSQPAHI/PSQPAHUN resolved onto qpah/qpahan/qpahi, all glossed 工作 — which is why all three had to be hand-pinned in HAND_NOT_UNGLOSSED. Respelled with the a they resolve onto psqapah / sqapah / qapah, the root the wordlist glosses 黏住（在）and 粘起來, which is his 黏貼－使黏附. Keyed on his RAW tokens psqpaxan/psqpaxe/psqpaxon — manual_map runs before normalisation, so keying it on the normalised psqpahan/psqpahi/psqpahun does nothing at all, silently.",
  "_sais_paradigm": "His SAIS 縫紉 paradigm line reads ° Smais, sais, sisi, sisan, sisun, and the derived slots drop the a. Modern Truku writes them with a long vowel instead: siisi (imperative patient focus), siisan (locative focus), siisun (patient focus irrealis), sniisan (preterite locative focus, the <n> infix). All four are in attested_modern.json and siisi/siisan also occur in the ILRDF parquets; NONE of his four spellings is listed at all. The bare root siis is not listed either, which is why no rule could ever reach this paradigm: the only glossed neighbour of `sisi` is `sisi` 用來濾酒的工具, the wine-strainer, a different word. That is the SISUN trap, and it was a SPELLING error the whole time, not a verification one. Ruled by a speaker, 2026-08-02.",
  "_salu_paradigm": "His S\"LU / SM\"LU cards (p. 284) are NOT the road root. He tagged both (R. = \"LU ?) and cross-referenced \"LU 路－通道－道理－方法 (p. 386), and the question mark is him being right to doubt: the root is SALU 'to make, to repair', an independent verb. Tgdaya salu = to make; smalu is the actor focus; snluwan is the preterite locative focus. Ruled by a speaker, 2026-08-03. Modern Truku has the whole paradigm already — salu 修理, smalu / smmalu 製作, snalu 用...做的, psalu 請…製造或修理, sluun 要被製作, and sluan / snluan listed unglossed; sluun is the proof that modern Truku writes the syncopated stem slu- exactly where he wrote S\"LU, so his \" is the reduced vowel of salu, not a glottal standing in for elu. We had been printing seelug / smeelug / sneelug / sneelugan — road words — on a card about making things, and two of them scored DARK because they are listed modern words. Same shape as the SISUN trap: a spelling error wearing a verification's clothes. \"LU itself is untouched: elu in Tgdaya, elug in modern Truku, and every form on that card is right.",
  "_saso_is_seesu": "SA'SO is SEESU [batch 159]. His root gloss is 沉靜－羞怯－羞恥心 and his paradigm is Msa'so 羞怯的－沉靜的－有禮的－知羞的 / Knsa'so 謙遜 / Psa'so 使平靜. The modern wordlist has that paradigm under `seesu`: mseesu 安靜, mgseesu 默默的;文靜, mnegseesu 文靜的, ttgseesu 溫柔；謙和, tgseesuay 使慎重, plus the bare knseesu / gseesu / tgseesu slots. Bare `seesu` is glossed 看輕人, which is the batch-154 肉/肥 and batch-157 化妞/銀 shape: the root's one-line gloss loses to its own paradigm. Only LISTED twins move; psa'so and pgsa'so stay pale because pseesu/pgseesu are unlisted. Keyed on his RAW tokens [batch 155].",
  "_the_final_g_class": "HIS TRANSCRIPTION DROPS A FINAL -g, as CLAUDE.md already records for 路 `elug` and 餵養 `tabug`. Four members go in, each confirmed by HIS OWN Chinese and not by the shape alone: `snpu` = `snpug` 數過；算過 (ini k'la snpu 沒辦法數了, ini k'la snpu patas 不識字), `msnulu` = `msnulug` 恰好 (Msnulu bi mstlong xea ludan 就在那一刻), `lubu` = `lubug` 音樂；聲響 and its `lmubu` = `lmubug` 彈琴, both under his LUBU 樂器. **`tabu` itself is refused** — there are TWO TABU entries, 餵養 and a hardwood, and this map is keyed on tokens, so respelling one would put a false dark spelling on the other. Same blocker as `bir`. `turu` and `nasu` are refused for want of a gloss of his and for homography.",
  "_winuk_is_hwinuk": "HIS OWN CROSS-REFERENCE. WINUK 腰－背部齊腰帶高度的部位（腎） carries the note 無疑是 XWINUK 的縮略形式；參 XWINUK — and X is his h, so XWINUK is `hwinuk` 腰部, already dark. He is not being corrected here; he is being taken at his word. The dictionary says the two are one entry, so the page spells them one way.",
